ure scan. Mask-interior coherence is higher for only 116/240 missed oracles and coherence-only subset mIoU 0.13079 versus B4 0.49186. Reconsider only with independent prospective evidence for a distinct mask-quality mechanism.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_l1_feature_consistency.py\", \"sha256\": \"146237155a756edde306694d2c18d1aefa7e1f895513e3f07550546b700c94c7\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-L1_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"f9d30c12b2ff6dc60caced2898efb89c459042239a5f50007cabeb6413b665df\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-L1-L2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-155700.md\", \"sha256\": \"589e282abaf2bcfdd488ad088bf5ae61da33912ab441b4b3b9f7041b35f599dc\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-L2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No admission or neighbor-count/fusion scan. Oracle boundary contrast higher in only 104/240 missed oracles and standalone subset mIoU 0.25651 versus B4 0.49186. Reconsider only with new prospective independent structural evidence.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_l1_feature_consistency.py\", \"sha256\": \"146237155a756edde306694d2c18d1aefa7e1f895513e3f07550546b700c94c7\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-L2_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"4e03775562c8deefe728819145bf3a37702fc702791b5f1b6985ce0aa9fb804e\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-L1-L2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-155700.md\", \"sha256\": \"589e282abaf2bcfdd488ad088bf5ae61da33912ab441b4b3b9f7041b35f599dc\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-J1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training admission. The fixed pooled-language contrast is higher for only 123/240 missed oracle queries, and standalone subset selection mIoU is 0.01315. Reconsider only with a distinct prospective diagnosis, not a validation feature or fusion-weight scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"9997360f5239c9aa8074bc0ad341e8ae6a6c33b23387d195dd5755005a0d0182\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-141100.md\", \"sha256\": \"648303bdf1c4e976aaa7d847869d03398d016e4cd96d4fcf7dc425cf1c1d4d3b\"},\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_j1_mask_language_evidence.py\", \"sha256\": \"fc152d7b9e99100a521e0ad6040194fa7e652e303a27fd14e0dd276480d725c4\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-J2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training admission. Only 78/240 missed oracles were more overlap-crowded than selected queries. Reconsider only if an independent, predeclared crowding mechanism has new evidence.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"9997360f5239c9aa8074bc0ad341e8ae6a6c33b23387d195dd5755005a0d0182\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-141100.md\", \"sha256\": \"648303bdf1c4e976aaa7d847869d03398d016e4cd96d4fcf7dc425cf1c1d4d3b\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-M1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training or seed-support threshold/fusion scan. Oracle support higher in only 48/240 material errors; support-only subset mIoU 0.43714 versus B4 0.49186. Reconsider only with independent prospective evidence for a distinct causal mechanism.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_m1_seed_support.py\", \"sha256\": \"e4dbf45b8ce05737e49f751e2e8a092856e9e0eb0b507fe4af738b517510d697\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-M1_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"2c18d9cf26edf916ee68b7fb944997ae854cceeefb389fe9e8d6fccd26c21734\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-M1-M2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-165700.md\", \"sha256\": \"96b2020ecac41fea7189bd4b8173c794c77ba72aaa8f1bd5a114885cedbc26dd\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-M2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training or appearance feature/fusion scan. Oracle 2D support higher in only 80/240 material errors; standalone subset mIoU 0.11752 versus B4 0.49186. Reconsider only with independent prospective evidence for a distinct causal mechanism.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_m2_appearance_support.py\", \"sha256\": \"c0e34ad784e24ae87f3f7a88cf1378585ab3ec1f2b6aebaabb0a846cd2fedec5\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-M2_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"5bdafd637beced25fbb02fe4de218ef636c508da83177382f8cd95e8ea5f4a08\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-M1-M2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-165700.md\", \"sha256\": \"96b2020ecac41fea7189bd4b8173c794c77ba72aaa8f1bd5a114885cedbc26dd\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-N1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not admit a detach-only ablation. Trained B4 mask/indicator gradient cosine varies from -0.868 to +0.194 over four fixed batches; a controlled single-parameter step has only a roughly 8e-7 mask-loss separation. Reconsider only with independent evidence for a distinct non-ablation mechanism and matched native control.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1-N3_diagnosis_20260926-183100.md\", \"sha256\": \"f4b71e7e2485a3281acbb15eea2d6802a2f39b4712eb65200fcbd3b3c0514cc9\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1_gradient_trained_b4_0_1.json\", \"sha256\": \"4cbbe2100b0c40006e358d740f7831dbfc442998a000a808f326ba3330e340fe\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1_gradient_trained_b4_64_65.json\", \"sha256\": \"56d3e167bd5ec90e5a1023d4460aead53b334d091f14ff2c8d02259d721483bb\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1_step_live_rng_0_1.json\", \"sha256\": \"a0e4a6230e296b1447ada549bb9c4fb429c58cc45a7861c5e9e7b039e2d0bef6\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1_step_detach_rng_0_1.json\", \"sha256\": \"0cdcf8ef4fc70264c5c8d8e551efcbacf2698e3b3e032faa5f7f36b43cf2a3f7\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-N2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training with oracle object IDs or validation-tuned language/mask grouping. Same-object selection inconsistency exists, but label-free nearest-language precision is 121/441 and overlapping-mask grouping is 171/354. Reconsider only on a prospectively justified inference-valid relation mechanism.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1-N3_diagnosis_20260926-183100.md\", \"sha256\": \"f4b71e7e2485a3281acbb15eea2d6802a2f39b4712eb65200fcbd3b3c0514cc9\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N2_language_proxy_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"1290b06e9ce4956a96e9723456f596f1bacc2603ba0a726ae56cf9379828335c\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N2_scene_consensus_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"afc9adb429aad8cb455ed87f5678df04af0f7442c8ff861eb59acaee2c962f21\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-N3\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not implement collision-only exclusivity loss. Native B4 yielded just 6/365 distinct-target pair collisions in 64 training scenes; reconsider only with independent evidence of a substantially different cross-expression confidence mechanism, not a loss-weight scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1-N3_diagnosis_20260926-183100.md\", \"sha256\": \"f4b71e7e2485a3281acbb15eea2d6802a2f39b4712eb65200fcbd3b3c0514cc9\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N3_collisions_64scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"562e2139756a4338b47ad6a4281db24e26ac1f94ee3d361ebeae5645ff3c52ba\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-O1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not admit token-masking confidence. Inference counterfactual changes expression semantics and reduced overall mIoU on train and validation; no matched semantic-preserving control. Reconsider only with a prospectively specified meaning-preserving intervention and native paired training diagnosis, not a token-position or fusion scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_o1_language_perturbation.py\", \"sha256\": \"ab26198f6b41e56536bd69b2a539212789cd1ad87158fa43894e6fd9e365e700\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"cc36895197a8142d4a09a7f2f58d1116d260bea635fe64db647291d3d1bbfc3d\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"a730f74c62907022a1161f0e0f9714b3103869168639e2990dfaefd68dac8db5\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-O2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not admit whole-appearance removal or a learned confidence gate derived from it. Removing all 2D features causes general distribution shift rather than error-specific evidence (422/455 query flips, mIoU 0.831 to 0.286). Reconsider only with independently justified localized modality evidence and a matched native control.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_o2_appearance_counterfactual.py\", \"sha256\": \"8db494c678768cf43bfa598ba980f2e56dfa303a745a812512097999919c3065\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O2_appearance_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"f1ee25ea70d463d306215f038ac8e2105c182b27b6f2555883fc8ed3adc3f42b\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-P1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No topology-confidence implementation or graph-degree scan. Oracle more connected in only 18/107 fixed training errors; topology-only mIoU 0.53896 vs B4 0.83083. Reconsider only with independent prospective causal evidence.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_p1_fragmentation.py\", \"sha256\": \"2e09c247782ccdbddf2c33ce2c0edaad067942d7708ee2bce08a16a99f17d5d4\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-P1_fragmentation_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"0fc2f4ba7e6eceaaf959d44773494a24f261aa16aea1572d8f9bdedf03d76b25\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-P2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No penultimate-layer swap or fusion scan. Recovered 0/107 fixed training errors; layer swap is pure ablation. Reconsider only with a distinct diagnosed computation path and all six gates.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_p2_confidence_trajectory.py\", \"sha256\": \"80612cec46d3e0de9dc604cc2fab8c86251dd2a8ed440641e6f2e3c7776bbf99\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-P2_confidence_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"5f2070f77062ba22612385af7f430fca04c8e5642ade0c197e6a953b4acd208b\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"design_cycle\": {\n    \"at\": \"2026-09-26T20:10:00+08:00\",\n    \"candidate_budget\": 2,\n    \"admitted\": 0,\n    \"attempted_ids\": [\"AdaRES-P1\", \"AdaRES-P2\"],\n    \"stop_reason\": \"independent_routes_exhausted\",\n    \"stop_detail\": \"P1 topology support had the wrong/absent direction in 107 training errors; P2 layer trajectory recovered none and a swap is pure ablation. Both fixed native probes disconfirmed their mechanisms before backward/resource gates. No other distinct evidence-backed executable route was identified in this bounded review; no global scientific exhaustion is claimed.\",\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-P1_fragmentation_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"0fc2f4ba7e6eceaaf959d44773494a24f261aa16aea1572d8f9bdedf03d76b25\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-P2_confidence_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"5f2070f77062ba22612385af7f430fca04c8e5642ade0c197e6a953b4acd208b\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-P1-P2_diagnosis_20260926-201000.md\", \"sha256\": \"0b577201b496d970db7d84a5637302c03266c901304e63bad9632df2429437f7\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-201000.md\", \"sha256\": \"54193f51b8272438e1167ecc4a5666989dd9af0e2f5b6593524483dde6f510ff\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-201000.md\", \"sha256\": \"9ec8f1066c9ab4172c53332067303d9bc558ee11525418fc13af3cf3446f71d9\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"cc36895197a8142d4a09a7f2f58d1116d260bea635fe64db647291d3d1bbfc3d\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"a730f74c62907022a1161f0e0f9714b3103869168639e2990dfaefd68dac8db5\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O2_appearance_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"f1ee25ea70d463d306215f038ac8e2105c182b27b6f2555883fc8ed3adc3f42b\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1-O2_diagnosis_20260926-190200.md\", \"sha256\": \"6ae221f02c0bbe7f6411e7f97411887bacacc233d2f5918b111d4f0e993c5cc8\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-190200.md\", \"sha256\": \"9ecca475bfc2f873fa995bcfaf10f0b47057db89a01f7004426f2c3c4a9610cf\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-190200.md\", \"sha256\": \"2b64089458f5c310375d2ca7e6067df18fc5e8ef5243883c0dadb0adadfb0e70\"}\n    ],\n    \"resume_condition\": \"Next capacity-gap tick: identify an independently justified inference-available metric-aligned confidence mechanism beyond P1/P2 and earlier rejected routes; freeze a paired native training control before backward/resources and all six admission gates. Reconcile any monitor/goal event first.\"\n  },\n  \"migration_notes\": \"AdaRES did not previously have research work tracking; B4 and B5 are the first explicit queued records.\"\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-201000.md -Raw; Get-Content pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-201000.md -Raw; Get-Content pipeline/reports/summary_20260926-201800.md -Raw'","aggregated_output":"# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 20:10 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Capacity gap 2/2; candidate budget 2. P1/P2 tested independent interpretations of inference-visible mask topology and confidence refinement.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| H5 | early stop | 0.5061 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n| G1 | complete | 0.4980 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nP1 oracle connectivity exceeded selected in only 18/107 errors; topology-only training mIoU 0.53896 versus B4 0.83083. P2 penultimate confidence recovered 0/107 errors and slightly lowered selected mIoU. Neither has diagnostic support for a metric-aligned confidence mechanism.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nNo trained candidate admitted. P1 is rejected for opposite/absent confidence direction. P2 is rejected as a layer-swap ablation with no error recovery. No model/config implementation or admission receipt. No validation threshold, graph-neighbor, layer-fusion or loss-weight search.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0/1 remain unassigned by this project's queue. A targeted pre-probe reading showed both idle (0% utilization, 1 MiB), not a claim about current occupancy. Server-6 excluded.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Fixed train-split native P1/P2 probes and repeat controls; raw outputs and hashes retained.\n- [x] Six gates assessed and failed at diagnosis/controls.\n- [ ] No backward, resource qualification, independent model package, receipt, sync, queue or training launch without a supported candidate.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nFixed 16 training scenes are not an efficacy or population estimate. P1 graph connectivity can depend on sampling density; varying graph degree on validation would be tuning. P2 float margins vary at exact equality despite stable discrete controls; no claim about confidence calibration or causal training effect.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nLayer swap, graph-neighbor scan, confidence fusion and new loss weight are pure ablation/tuning variants, not structurally independent mechanisms. Neither passes the three structural and causal standards for admission.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Bounded P1/P2 executable diagnoses disconfirmed; no global exhaustion claim.\n\r\n# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 20:10 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nAdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 baseline 0.5020; B4-E30 champion 0.5094, gap 0.0056. Goal constraints: server-2 GPUs 0/1 only, one independent task each, released backbone and project decoder, fixed B2/B4 continuation, report mIoU/Acc@0.25/Acc@0.5/active queries/latency/peak memory, no validation tuning of thresholds, temperatures, weights, features or epochs. Bans: server-6, released checkpoint as B0, ranking-margin or occupancy-weight validation scans.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Competition-aware confidence | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Below target; oracle selection headroom |\n| Metric-IoU targets | Negative | G1 0.4980 | No target/weight scan |\n| Spatial fragmentation evidence | Negative | P1 oracle more connected 18/107 train errors | No reliable confidence direction |\n| Layer-trajectory evidence | Negative | P2 recovers 0/107 train errors | Layer swap is an ablation |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 0.5020, B4-E30 0.5094, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061, G1 0.4980. P1/P2 were native inference diagnoses, not trained experiments; previous O1/O2 were rejected as semantic-changing and global-shift interventions.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nInference-visible evidence that identifies a missed high-IoU query without oracle labels remains unverified. P1 spatial connectedness and P2 confidence depth do not resolve this gap. Active queries, latency and full-run peak memory remain unavailable for historical variants.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nP1 tested a topology mechanism distinct from compactness/boundary features; P2 tested whether iterative indicator refinement itself discarded a correct selection. Both used frozen training-cohort readouts and repeat controls. Neither supports a new computational confidence pathway. Their negative results narrow the bounded routes but not the overall research space.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-201000.md`. Independent future route requires metric-aligned diagnosis, matched native control, backward/resources, independence and goal compliance.\n\r\n================================================================================\n  Research Pipeline Report - AdaRES_project\n  2026-09-26 20:18 Asia/Shanghai (design tick)\n================================================================================\n\n## 0. Goal Status\n| Target | Champion | Gap | Phase |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.5150 | AdaRES-B4-E30 0.5094 | 0.0056 | Phase 1 unmet; Phase 2 pending |\n\nB1 baseline 0.5020; champion gain +0.0074. Prepared monitor/goal preflight succeeded once and was not rerun.\n\n## 1. GPU Overview\n| Server | GPU | Util | Memory Used | Assignment |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| server-2 | 0 | 0% before probes | 1 MiB before probes | no project task; P1/P2 probes completed |\n| server-2 | 1 | 0% before probes | 1 MiB before probes | no project task |\n\nNo current occupancy conclusion follows from the pre-probe reading. Server-6 excluded.\n\n## 2. Running Experiments\n| ID | Config | Server | GPU | Epoch | Best mIoU | Acc@50 | spmIoU | No-Impr | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| - | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | none |\n\n## 3. Queue Status\n| Position | ID | Config | Status | Depends On | Server |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| - | - | - | no waiting or claiming tasks | - | - |\n\nActive 0/2 target; candidate budget 2. Neither P1 nor P2 passed diagnosis/controls gates. No due research candidates.\n\n## 4. This Tick's Actions\n- P1 fixed 16 training-scene topology diagnosis with repeat control: 455 expressions, 107 material errors, oracle more connected in 18; topology-only mIoU 0.53896 versus indicator 0.83083.\n- P2 independent final/penultimate indicator diagnosis on the same cohort: 24 selections changed, zero material errors recovered, mIoU 0.830827 versus 0.830534. Repeat discrete mismatch 0; initial exact-float mismatch was a control-metric artifact and corrected.\n- Preserved raw outputs, scripts, analysis, motivation review, design and hashed research ledger. Inference peak reserved memory 3.46 GiB is not training peak. No native backward, implementation, receipt, sync, dispatch or queue mutation.\n- No pending questions in prepared snapshot. Resume on a distinct inference-available confidence mechanism with frozen paired native control and all six gates; bounded P1/P2 exhaustion is not global scientific exhaustion.\n\n## 5. Decisions Made\n- 2026-09-26 20:17 `route_change`: reject P1/P2, leave server-2 GPU0/1 unqueued. See `pipeline/decisions/20260926-201727_route_change.md`.\n\n================================================================================\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
